{"data":[{"author_id":"279036722","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:30:21.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112310409671688690"],"id":"2112310409671688690","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":176,"impression_count":88612,"like_count":719,"quote_count":51,"reply_count":64,"retweet_count":122},"text":"The fatal challenge to heterodox economics is that there isn't actually orthodox economics.\n\nJust take a few recent Nobels: behavioral, information failure, institutions, bubbles, financial fragility, labor monopsony (sort of), Schumpeterian creative destruction, etc.\n\nNot to","url":"https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2112310409671688690"},{"author_id":"1214528593","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:25:53.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112309287448084708"],"id":"2112309287448084708","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":2382,"like_count":15,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":2},"text":"Tis the season to meet the moment","url":"https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2112309287448084708"},{"author_id":"1214528593","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:06:40.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112304449708544406"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/fiiiiiist/stat…","end":72,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/fiiiiiist/status/2112262515531137121","start":49,"url":"https://t.co/AshPj4SZkI"}]},"id":"2112304449708544406","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":7,"impression_count":4257,"like_count":33,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":5,"retweet_count":5},"text":"Good ideas on how to 🇺🇸 🤜 💥 on 🤖 \n\nFrom 🤜 et al. https://t.co/AshPj4SZkI","url":"https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2112304449708544406"},{"author_id":"39125788","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:07:38.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112289593286352976"],"id":"2112289593286352976","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":156,"impression_count":41856,"like_count":467,"quote_count":26,"reply_count":188,"retweet_count":22},"text":"Multiplayer AI needs to move past the group chat phase. Chats are chaotic, everyone sees everything (creating social &amp; management issues), and they're bad for long projects. Worse, they keep AI trapped inside existing teams, when its real promise is working &amp; helping across them.","url":"https://x.com/emollick/status/2112289593286352976"},{"author_id":"1214528593","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:16:28.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112276717800919504"],"id":"2112276717800919504","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":1,"impression_count":2951,"like_count":6,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Really dumb Uber feature: losing the ability to communicate with the driver during a multi-stop trip","url":"https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2112276717800919504"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112271760200749056"]},"author_id":"332617373","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:56:54.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112271794673717707"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/tvWJsbbCSz","end":223,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112271794673717707/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112271760200749056","start":200,"url":"https://t.co/tvWJsbbCSz"}]},"id":"2112271794673717707","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":2,"impression_count":34268,"like_count":193,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":24,"retweet_count":4},"text":"Every time I see this simple setup on an airplane—a foot pedal to open the bin flap—I can’t help wondering why more airlines don’t adopt it. It’s so much more convenient for passengers, and hygienic. https://t.co/tvWJsbbCSz","url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112271794673717707"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2112247274852257792","3_2112247274835517440","3_2112247274831216640","3_2112247274822868993"]},"author_id":"332617373","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:19:50.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112247364950032812"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":271,"start":267,"tag":"ypo"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/8owbTvgF7b","end":295,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112247364950032812/video/1","media_key":"13_2112247274852257792","start":272,"url":"https://t.co/8owbTvgF7b"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/8owbTvgF7b","end":295,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112247364950032812/video/1","media_key":"3_2112247274835517440","start":272,"url":"https://t.co/8owbTvgF7b"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/8owbTvgF7b","end":295,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112247364950032812/video/1","media_key":"3_2112247274831216640","start":272,"url":"https://t.co/8owbTvgF7b"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/8owbTvgF7b","end":295,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112247364950032812/video/1","media_key":"3_2112247274822868993","start":272,"url":"https://t.co/8owbTvgF7b"}]},"id":"2112247364950032812","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":2,"impression_count":33940,"like_count":103,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":6,"retweet_count":4},"text":"Such a pleasure to speak at the YPO event in Beverly Hills! Thank you. And thank you, Betty Liu, for the interesting conversation.\nFirst time being introduced via an AI-generated video! Plus, being at the iconic Beverly Wilshire meant a fun \"Pretty Woman\" theme too.\n#ypo https://t.co/8owbTvgF7b","url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112247364950032812"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112238506898534401"]},"author_id":"26538229","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:45:03.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112238612087439670"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":29,"start":5,"tag":"FederalReserveEducation"},{"end":82,"start":70,"tag":"EconEdMonth"}],"urls":[{"description":"Join Federal Reserve Education in recognizing National Economic Education Month for a webinar on the implementation of monetary policy. During this virtual event, attendees will learn about the evolution of monetary policy from the origins of the Federal Reserve System to the modern day. We will also introduce the new monetary policy comic, How Does Monetary Policy Work?, and share activities on using Federal Open Market Committee data releases in the classroom. There is no cost to attend, but registration","display_url":"cvent.me/BA02Rb","end":235,"expanded_url":"https://cvent.me/BA02Rb","images":[{"height":1054,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109731853699563521/8DgKKkVb?format=png&name=orig","width":1054},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2109731853699563521/8DgKKkVb?format=png&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":212,"status":200,"title":"Your Registration Information - Teaching Monetary Policy: From the Fed’s Origins to Today’s Tools","unwound_url":"https://web.cvent.com/event/ca4a90ad-55ef-40b4-96cf-2399d475ab8d/register","url":"https://t.co/tb5oTBW7hT"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/fzbtIrIJrK","end":260,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2112238612087439670/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112238506898534401","start":237,"url":"https://t.co/fzbtIrIJrK"}]},"id":"2112238612087439670","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":8,"impression_count":28657,"like_count":41,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":15,"retweet_count":10},"text":"Join #FederalReserveEducation on Tuesday, October 20, as we celebrate #EconEdMonth with our webinar, Teaching Monetary Policy: From the Fed’s Origins to Today’s Tools. For more information and to register, visit https://t.co/tb5oTBW7hT. https://t.co/fzbtIrIJrK","url":"https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2112238612087439670"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112212242959917056"]},"author_id":"25098482","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:39.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112212591548506281"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":87,"id":"123109597","start":76,"username":"KGeorgieva"}],"urls":[{"description":"AI promises a more productive world, but we must manage risks in the transition","display_url":"imf.org/en/blogs/artic…","end":172,"expanded_url":"https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2026/10/15/the-world-cant-afford-to-get-ai-wrong","images":[{"height":600,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2110854510503694337/Ew_c017W?format=jpg&name=orig","width":2099},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2110854510503694337/Ew_c017W?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":149,"status":200,"title":"The World Can’t Afford to Get AI Wrong","unwound_url":"https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2026/10/15/the-world-cant-afford-to-get-ai-wrong","url":"https://t.co/HxSKGgWLjm"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/sWQfI5r1O9","end":196,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2112212591548506281/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112212242959917056","start":173,"url":"https://t.co/sWQfI5r1O9"}]},"id":"2112212591548506281","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":7,"impression_count":21606,"like_count":59,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":8,"retweet_count":13},"text":"AI promises a more productive world, but we must manage the transition. See @KGeorgieva's latest blog on why the world can’t afford to get AI wrong: https://t.co/HxSKGgWLjm https://t.co/sWQfI5r1O9","url":"https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2112212591548506281"},{"author_id":"39125788","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:53:44.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112210597571862980"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"The new book from Ethan Mollick, author of Co-Intelligence. Available now.","display_url":"co-existence.ai","end":287,"expanded_url":"https://co-existence.ai/","images":[{"height":1510,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112580750046633987/YJXvr9Ai?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1000},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112580750046633987/YJXvr9Ai?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":264,"status":200,"title":"Co-Existence: The Next Phase of AI","unwound_url":"https://co-existence.ai/","url":"https://t.co/Ti5jo6ksfI"}]},"id":"2112210597571862980","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":54,"impression_count":19530,"like_count":247,"quote_count":4,"reply_count":32,"retweet_count":20},"text":"My book comes out tomorrow, so this is the last day to qualify for the pre-order bonus: a fun 10 minute AI voice interview that gives you personalized prompts, ideas, &amp; readings based on ideas from the book\n\nYou can order &amp; claim the pre-order bonus here: https://t.co/Ti5jo6ksfI","url":"https://x.com/emollick/status/2112210597571862980"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112202774536450048"]},"author_id":"612896910","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:30:00.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112204628083294290"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":73,"start":65,"tag":"BLSData"}],"urls":[{"description":"The .gov means it's official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you're on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. Nuclear Science Week, the third week of October, highlights the contributions of nuclear technology to fields as varied as agriculture, electric power generation, and healthcar","display_url":"bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/…","end":97,"expanded_url":"https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/recognizing-nuclear-science-occupations-for-nuclear-science-week.htm","images":[{"height":126,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112204671729205248/Awj9iedq?format=png&name=orig","width":228},{"height":126,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112204671729205248/Awj9iedq?format=png&name=150x150","width":126}],"start":74,"status":200,"title":"Recognizing nuclear science occupations for Nuclear Science Week : The Economics Daily : U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics","unwound_url":"https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/recognizing-nuclear-science-occupations-for-nuclear-science-week.htm","url":"https://t.co/haCpXr6EyO"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/G8VQd6es02","end":121,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2112204628083294290/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112202774536450048","start":98,"url":"https://t.co/G8VQd6es02"}]},"id":"2112204628083294290","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":3,"impression_count":2645,"like_count":8,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":2,"retweet_count":3},"text":"Recognizing nuclear science occupations for Nuclear Science Week #BLSData https://t.co/haCpXr6EyO https://t.co/G8VQd6es02","url":"https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2112204628083294290"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112187773998583808"]},"author_id":"332617373","created_at":"2026-10-19T14:23:05.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112187785109201168"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/kFHxbUiNfi","end":302,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112187785109201168/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112187773998583808","start":279,"url":"https://t.co/kFHxbUiNfi"}]},"id":"2112187785109201168","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":53,"impression_count":55217,"like_count":557,"quote_count":22,"reply_count":63,"retweet_count":131},"text":"Good morning.\nOf note: French bond yields have been surging today (Bloomberg chart), pulling European peers higher and spilling over somewhat into the US.\nAs noted previously, this dynamic is worth monitoring: if it gains traction, and it's an IF, the resulting two-way feedback https://t.co/kFHxbUiNfi","url":"https://x.com/elerianm/status/2112187785109201168"},{"author_id":"279036722","created_at":"2026-10-19T13:40:15.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112177008511729730"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/jasonfurman/st…","end":264,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/jasonfurman/status/2111497517858685190","start":241,"url":"https://t.co/ActOYAcTHW"}]},"id":"2112177008511729730","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":18,"impression_count":17321,"like_count":103,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":3,"retweet_count":9},"text":"There have been 27 international Bank-Fund meetings since 1947, generally one every three years.\n\nThe U.S. Treasury Secretary attended 26 of the 27.\n\nAnd no one seemed that surprised or disappointed that the Treasury didn't attend this one. https://t.co/ActOYAcTHW","url":"https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2112177008511729730"},{"author_id":"68746721","created_at":"2026-10-19T13:06:49.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112168594352349518"],"id":"2112168594352349518","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":92,"impression_count":44145,"like_count":797,"quote_count":9,"reply_count":81,"retweet_count":50},"text":"When enough people believe something will happen, it doesn't need to happen at all for all of its consequences to be felt","url":"https://x.com/fchollet/status/2112168594352349518"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112165207468331009"]},"author_id":"39125788","created_at":"2026-10-19T12:53:23.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112165213202157907"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"Large language models increasingly write the code behind empirical research. This column reports a benchmark of 40 econometric tasks in Stata, R, and Python. For each task, two leading models write a script, as a chatbot that never runs it and as an agent that runs and revises it. Letting the models run their code raises the share of correct results from 79% to 97% and makes the prompt and the software matter far less. The failures that remain under the agent come from scripts that run without errors but return wrong numbers, and detecting them is still the researcher’s work.","display_url":"cepr.org/voxeu/columns/…","end":279,"expanded_url":"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/letting-ai-agents-write-econometric-code","images":[{"height":675,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111596101744680960/91oP2xFj?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1200},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111596101744680960/91oP2xFj?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":256,"status":200,"title":"Letting AI agents write econometric code","unwound_url":"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/letting-ai-agents-write-econometric-code","url":"https://t.co/8Qk6VgU7w8"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/Wl1zUqbt0j","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/emollick/status/2112165213202157907/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112165207468331009","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/Wl1zUqbt0j"}]},"id":"2112165213202157907","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":169,"impression_count":48597,"like_count":431,"quote_count":22,"reply_count":162,"retweet_count":64},"text":"Writing good STATA code was very important for my academic career. It looks like that skill is largely becoming obsolete. (Also take this is as a notice to academics who still think of AI in terms of chatbots, not agents, that a lot has changed in a year) https://t.co/8Qk6VgU7w8 https://t.co/Wl1zUqbt0j","url":"https://x.com/emollick/status/2112165213202157907"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112151895426920448"]},"author_id":"321536046","created_at":"2026-10-19T12:00:30.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112151906239844595"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":106,"start":96,"tag":"AUBER2026"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/qyHkGnFTFs","end":130,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2112151906239844595/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112151895426920448","start":107,"url":"https://t.co/qyHkGnFTFs"}]},"id":"2112151906239844595","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":910,"like_count":2,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"AUBER conference attendees: Stop by our booth today to learn the latest about BEA econ data! \n \n#AUBER2026 https://t.co/qyHkGnFTFs","url":"https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2112151906239844595"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["16_2112143933551869952"]},"author_id":"25098482","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:28:58.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112143970449097025"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":225,"id":"827641479220883457","start":213,"username":"jihad_azour"},{"end":263,"id":"49556187","start":258,"username":"DIFC"}],"urls":[{"description":"Steering Through Uncertainty: Strengthening Resilience in Challenging Times","display_url":"x.com/i/broadcasts/1…","end":288,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/i/broadcasts/1AKEmvaVzdYKL","images":[{"height":675,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112130708428951552/BPpBQJpu?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1200},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112130708428951552/BPpBQJpu?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":265,"status":200,"title":"IMF Middle East & North Africa","unwound_url":"https://x.com/i/broadcasts/1AKEmvaVzdYKL","url":"https://t.co/quU4ibPv8A"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/S6D1MGBzQU","end":312,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2112143970449097025/photo/1","media_key":"16_2112143933551869952","start":289,"url":"https://t.co/S6D1MGBzQU"}]},"id":"2112143970449097025","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":2,"impression_count":25147,"like_count":49,"quote_count":2,"reply_count":4,"retweet_count":8},"text":"Save the Date: Oct 22. How is the MENA region weathering recent shocks &amp; persistent uncertainty? Join us for the launch of the IMF's Oct 2026 Regional Economic Outlook, Steering Through Uncertainty, featuring @jihad_azour &amp; leading experts hosted by @DIFC.\nhttps://t.co/quU4ibPv8A https://t.co/S6D1MGBzQU","url":"https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2112143970449097025"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112121581573132288"]},"author_id":"25098482","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:00:45.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112121769016648096"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"The Regional Economic Outlook Update: Sub-Saharan Africa will be available on October 15, 2026 (4:30 PM UTC+7).","display_url":"imf.org/en/publication…","end":279,"expanded_url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/reo/ssa/issues/2026/10/15/regional-economic-outlook-for-sub-saharan-africa-october-2026?cid=sm-com-x-am26-REOAFREA2026002","images":[{"height":405,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111721494107844608/s9AdOemk?format=png&name=orig","width":400},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111721494107844608/s9AdOemk?format=png&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":256,"status":200,"title":"Regional Economic Outlook Update: Sub-Saharan Africa, October 2026","unwound_url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/reo/ssa/issues/2026/10/15/regional-economic-outlook-for-sub-saharan-africa-october-2026?cid=sm-com-x-am26-REOAFREA2026002","url":"https://t.co/YpCvzdZ28v"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/F53ae7Hxsy","end":303,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2112121769016648096/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112121581573132288","start":280,"url":"https://t.co/F53ae7Hxsy"}]},"id":"2112121769016648096","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":4,"impression_count":23235,"like_count":81,"quote_count":7,"reply_count":15,"retweet_count":20},"text":"Sub-Saharan Africa’s growth remains resilient but uneven. The IMF projects growth of 4.5% in 2026 and 2027, while median inflation rises to 4.3% this year. Policies should ensure price stability and rebuild buffers, while supporting vulnerable households. https://t.co/YpCvzdZ28v https://t.co/F53ae7Hxsy","url":"https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2112121769016648096"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2112106932865576960"]},"author_id":"83466368","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:02:44.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112107169298407712"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/webI1ky4I4","end":282,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/ecb/status/2112107169298407712/photo/1","media_key":"3_2112106932865576960","start":259,"url":"https://t.co/webI1ky4I4"}]},"id":"2112107169298407712","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":8,"impression_count":8853,"like_count":43,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":4,"retweet_count":17},"text":"From Keynes’s famous “digging holes” example to modern stabilisation policy, Economics has come a long way in understanding how governments can respond to crises. \n\nThe 2026 Nobel Prize recognises that progress. This blog post explains the research behind it https://t.co/webI1ky4I4","url":"https://x.com/ecb/status/2112107169298407712"},{"author_id":"1214528593","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:05:24.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2112092741392040118"],"id":"2112092741392040118","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":3709,"like_count":45,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":9,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Who called it the web of fiber 